      "text": "The script finds the first \"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\" block, reads the four needed columns (SMALL LoINV, BIG LoINV, SMALL HiINV, BIG HiINV), and computes CMA = 0.5\u00b7(Small Lo + Big Lo) \u2212 0.5\u00b7(Small Hi + Big Hi). Missing-value codes (-99.99, -999) are treated as NaN and those months are dropped. Parsing stops at the first non-date line after the block, so the later tables are never read.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport csv\n\nFILE = \"6_Portfolios_ME_INV_2x3.csv\"\nOUT = \"output.csv\"\n\n\ndef norm(s):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", s.strip()).upper()\n\n\ndef to_float(tok):\n    try:\n        v = float(tok)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return float(\"nan\")\n    if v in (-99.99, -999.0) or v != v:\n        return float(\"nan\")\n    return v\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(FILE, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.readlines()\n\n    # locate first (value-weighted, monthly) block\n    start = None\n    for i, l in enumerate(lines):\n        if \"Value Weighted Returns\" in l and \"Monthly\" in l:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Monthly value-weighted block not found\")\n\n    # header line: first non-empty line after the title\n    j = start + 1\n    while j < len(lines) and not lines[j].strip():\n        j += 1\n    header = [norm(h) for h in lines[j].strip().split(\",\")]\n\n    want = {\n        \"SMALL LOINV\": None,\n        \"BIG LOINV\": None,\n        \"SMALL HIINV\": None,\n        \"BIG HIINV\": None,\n    }\n    for idx, h in enumerate(header):\n        if h in want:\n            want[h] = idx\n    missing = [k for k, v in want.items() if v is None]\n    if missing:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Missing columns: {missing}\")\n\n    rows = []\n    for l in lines[j + 1:]:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in l.strip().split(\",\")]\n        if not parts or not re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", parts[0] or \"\"):\n            break  # end of the monthly block\n        date = int(parts[0])\n\n        def get(name):\n            k = want[name]\n            return to_float(parts[k]) if k < len(parts) else float(\"nan\")\n\n        sl = get(\"SMALL LOINV\")\n        bl = get(\"BIG LOINV\")\n        sh = get(\"SMALL HIINV\")\n        bh = get(\"BIG HIINV\")\n        vals = (sl, bl, sh, bh)\n        if any(v != v for v in vals):\n            continue\n        cma = 0.5 * (sl + bl) - 0.5 * (sh + bh)\n        rows.append((date, cma))\n\n    with open(OUT, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for d, v in rows:\n            w.writerow([d, f\"{v:.6f}\"])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
